  "source": "",
  "lolo": "app std-patrol-hazard \"1.0.0\"\n\"Headless patrol-hazard mechanic for side-view boards: moves each configured patrol back and forth along its [x0, x1] beat at its own speed (33ms tick, ping-pong with clamped turnarounds; a patrol declaring waveAmp/wavePeriod also bobs vertically — cy = y + waveAmp·sin(2πt/wavePeriod from a per-row time accumulator — and the hit test and render read cy, so a waveAmp of 0 keeps the flat beat), tracks the player position off the body authority's BODY_MOVED, and emits PATROL_HIT once per contact — a per-patrol hit flag re-arms only after the player separates, so damage rules stay sparse (when two patrols connect on the same tick the first reports; the other reports on the next tick). Patrols live on a [runtime, shared] entity for the render layer (boards draw them as markers/sprites); damage, lives, and respawn stay downstream (std-lives) — this atom simulates, it never judges. SET_PATROLS replaces the live patrol set at runtime for boards that import their patrols; RESTART re-arms the live set, so injected patrols survive respawns. Renders nothing. Corresponds to the design-sheet field(s): challenge, dynamics.\"\norbital PatrolHazardOrbital {\n  type Patrol = {\n    id : string!\n    x0 : number!\n    x1 : number!\n    y : number!\n    speed : number!\n    waveAmp : number\n    wavePeriod : number\n    x : number\n    dir : number\n    t : number\n    cy : number\n    touching : boolean\n    hit : boolean\n  }\n\n  entity PatrolState [runtime, shared] {\n    id : string!\n    patrols : [Patrol] = []\n    px : number = 0\n    py : number = 0\n  }\n\n  trait PatrolHazard -> @rebindable PatrolState [lifecycle] {\n    initial: active\n\n    state active {\n      INIT -> active\n        (set @entity.patrols (array/map @config.patrols (fn p (object/merge @p { x: (object/get @p x0), dir: 1, t: 0, cy: (object/get @p y), touching: false, hit: false }))))\n        (set @entity.px @config.playerSpawnX)\n        (set @entity.py @config.playerSpawnY)\n\n      BODY_MOVED -> active\n        (set @entity.px @payload.x)\n        (set @entity.py @payload.y)\n\n      SET_PATROLS -> active\n        (set @entity.patrols (array/map @payload.patrols (fn p (object/merge @p { x: (object/get @p x0), dir: 1, t: 0, cy: (object/get @p y), touching: false, hit: false }))))\n        (set @entity.px @config.playerSpawnX)\n        (set @entity.py @config.playerSpawnY)\n\n      RESTART -> active\n        (set @entity.patrols (array/map @entity.patrols (fn p (object/merge @p { x: (object/get @p x0), dir: 1, t: 0, cy: (object/get @p y), touching: false, hit: false }))))\n    }\n\n    ticks {\n      patrolTick every 33ms\n        when (and @config.running (> (array/len @entity.patrols) 0))\n        (set @entity.patrols (array/map @entity.patrols (fn p\n          (let ((nx (+ (object/get @p x) (* (* (object/get @p dir) (object/get @p speed)) 0.033))))\n          (let ((overshoot (> @nx (object/get @p x1))) (undershoot (< @nx (object/get @p x0))))\n          (let ((cx (if @overshoot (object/get @p x1) (if @undershoot (object/get @p x0) @nx)))\n                (cdir (if @overshoot -1 (if @undershoot 1 (object/get @p dir)))))\n          (let ((nt (+ (object/get @p t) 0.033)))\n          (let ((amp (if (== (object/get @p waveAmp) null) 0 (object/get @p waveAmp))) (period (if (== (object/get @p wavePeriod) null) 3 (object/get @p wavePeriod))))\n          (let ((cy (+ (object/get @p y) (* @amp (math/sin (/ (* 6.283185307179586 @nt) @period))))))\n          (let ((near (and (<= (math/abs (- @entity.px @cx)) @config.hitRadius) (<= (math/abs (- @entity.py @cy)) @config.hitRadius))))\n            (object/merge @p { x: @cx, dir: @cdir, t: @nt, cy: @cy, hit: (and @near (== (object/get @p touching) false)), touching: @near })))))))))))\n        (let ((hits (array/filter @entity.patrols (fn p (== (object/get @p hit) true)))))\n        (if (> (array/len @hits) 0)\n          (emit PATROL_HIT { id: (object/get (array/first @hits) id), x: (object/get (array/first @hits) x), y: (object/get (array/first @hits) cy) })\n          null))\n    }\n\n    emits {\n      PATROL_HIT -> external {\n        id : string!\n        x : number!\n        y : number!\n      }\n        @description \"A patrol made contact with the player this tick; fires once per contact and re-arms only after separation — boards route it to their damage rule (std-lives DAMAGE).\"\n        @tier \"domain\"\n    }\n\n    listens {\n      BODY_MOVED { x : number!, y : number!, vx : number!, vy : number!, grounded : boolean!, skating : boolean!, speed : number! }\n      SET_PATROLS { patrols : [Patrol]! }\n      RESTART { id : string }\n    }\n\n    config {\n      running : boolean = true\n        @label \"Running\"\n        @description \"When true the 33ms tick moves patrols and tests contact; toggle to freeze every patrol in place.\"\n        @tier \"domain\"\n      patrols : [Patrol] = []\n        @label \"Patrols\"\n        @description \"One row per patroller: id, the [x0, x1] beat it walks, its base y, its speed in units/s, and optionally waveAmp/wavePeriod for a vertical sine bob (waveAmp 0 = flat ping-pong). Current x/dir/t/cy/touching/hit are stamped at runtime. Seeded onto the entity on INIT; the live set is entity.patrols — SET_PATROLS replaces it at runtime (boards that import patrols), and RESTART re-arms the live set rather than re-reading config, so injected patrols survive respawns.\"\n        @tier \"domain\"\n      hitRadius : number = 0.7\n        @label \"Hit Radius\"\n        @description \"Per-axis distance (world units) within which a patrol counts as touching the player; smaller values demand precise contact, larger values forgive.\"\n        @tier \"domain\"\n      playerSpawnX : number = 0\n        @label \"Player Spawn X\"\n        @description \"Player x assumed before the first BODY_MOVED arrives (match the body authority's spawn).\"\n        @tier \"domain\"\n      playerSpawnY : number = 0\n        @label \"Player Spawn Y\"\n        @description \"Player y assumed before the first BODY_MOVED arrives.\"\n        @tier \"domain\"\n    }\n  }\n\n  page \"/patrol-hazard\" as PatrolHazardPage -> PatrolHazard\n}\n"
}